{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation on this trip is established but NOT material, and that caps everything that follows. The governing measurement is the trace rather than the rounded copy of it: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 23.97 km against a booked optimal of 18.0 km, an excess of 5.97 km and 33.17%. That passes both POL-RD-01 establishment gates of 0.8 km and 20%, so the rider is right that a deviation exists and I do not pretend otherwise. But it fails both materiality gates: 5.97 km is under the 8.0 km figure and 33.17% is under the 50% figure. The consequence is that no POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is required, no FULL_REFUND uplift is available, and no conduct referral arises on this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Concession, and it is a real one: the driver does not discharge the POL-RD-08 burden. His own counterparty statement says 'No advisory that I know of'; the chat log contains only 'AYE jam boss, this way faster', with waypoint_hint null on both messages; and the single traffic-advisory artifact on the case, EV-ADVIS-00114-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. I disclose that impairment rather than dress it up. POL-RD-03 requires an advisory naming a road, a validity window and a matched deviation around the affected segment; with no advisory at all, limbs (a) to (c) cannot be run and no exoneration attaches to the driver's route choice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00114-01", "EV-CHAT-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "counterparty_statement",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The one excusable explanation the driver offers is the one the record cannot test, and that matters for the disposition. The driver asserts the AYE was crawling from the Alexandra exit, and the artifact that would have decided that assertion — EV-ADVIS-00114-01 — is MISSING with weight 0.0 and carries a BLOCKING issue detail recording that no LTA advisory covers the AYE, the PIE or the Alexandra corridor in the 18:36-19:20 window. POL-RD-10(5) names precisely this situation, 'a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory', and directs escalation rather than a monetary ruling. On that reading the exoneration question is undecidable on this record, the case goes to a human with the disputed amount held rather than refunded, and I ask the chamber to prefer that route over a confident ruling on an incomplete record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00114-01", "EV-CHAT-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "counterparty_statement",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "If the chamber rules on the money, the surge must be carried at the figure the artifact records, not at zero. POL-RD-02 requires the multiplier to be read from the fare_breakdown, where it is 1.6, and applied to the whole optimal base of 25.70 (3.80 base + 0.75 x 18.0 = 13.50 distance + 0.28 x 30.0 = 8.40 time). That adds 15.42 of surge uplift to the recomputed fare and takes the same 15.42 off the refund. A recomputation that quietly dropped the surge would refund the rider for a surge he expressly told the platform he accepts.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.surge_uplift",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The remedy is arithmetic and it is well below both the rider's demand and the charge. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 18.0 + 0.28 x 30.0) x 1.6) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.50 of on-route ERP = 44.42, against a charged_total of 58.10. The refund is therefore 13.68, payable 13.70 once rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 under POL-RD-02 — not the 15.00 the rider contests and nowhere near the 58.10 full refund. The refund is 23.5% of the charge, far below the 90% share that would make it a FULL_REFUND, and it is above the 0.50 de minimis floor so the rider does take something. The 1.30 by which the rider's figure exceeds the arithmetic corresponds to no line of the fare_breakdown, and POL-RD-02 does not permit a discretionary top-up to a round number.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's $4.50 ERP complaint is wrong by half and is in any event already paid for by the refund above. Of the two charged lines, only the Adam Road gantry at $2.00 is off the optimal route; the Kim Keat Link gantry at $2.50 is on the optimal route, and the driver's trace passes it at a nearest fix of 0.0 m. The POL-RD-02 recomputation therefore carries the 2.50 inside the recomputed fare and leaves the 2.00 out, which means the off-route ERP is already comprehended in the 13.68 refund. Under POL-RD-09(1) that line is itemised for transparency but must never be added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, so the rider recovers the off-route gantry once and not twice.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114", "EV-GPS-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_lines.off_optimal_route_total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no billing-integrity defect here and no standalone correction is due. Both billed gantries are matched to the trace well inside the 250 m crossing radius that POL-RD-09(4) uses — Kim Keat Link at a nearest fix of 0.0 m and Adam Road at 8.76 m — so neither is a phantom line and no line is refundable under that limb. Nor is the trace impaired for policy purposes: coverage is 100% over 241 fixes at a 10 second interval, with no gaps, a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, no jump over 500 m and no sustained interval above 30 seconds, so POL-RD-07 does not bite and the excess stands on the trace alone without need of independent corroboration.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00114", "EV-FARE-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-06 stays shut on this trip's own numbers. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1, below the three-flag trigger the clause sets, and 1 flag over driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 412 is a ratio of about 0.0024, far below the 0.05 ratio the clause requires with at least 40 completed trips. Neither limb of the pattern test is met, and the deviation is not material in any event. No repeat-pattern finding, no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) can be built on this profile — and POL-GEN-01 forbids using any other field on the profile, such as the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter, to do the work this test cannot.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 13.70,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties — the arithmetic here is not seriously in dispute, and the record supports a partial refund to the rider.\n\nTHE DEVIATION. The governing measurement is the trace, not the rounded copy: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 23.97 km against the booked optimal of 18.0 km, an excess of 5.97 km (33.2%). Both POL-RD-01 establishment gates pass (over 0.8 km and over 20%), so a deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not a MATERIAL deviation — 5.97 km is under the 8.0 km gate and 33.2% is under the 50% gate — so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile review, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral arise. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (241 fixes, 10-second interval, 100% coverage, zero gaps, no jumps over 500 m), so the finding stands on the trace alone and needs no independent corroboration.\n\nTHE MONEY (POL-RD-02, read on the METERED fare_breakdown).\n- Charged total: SGD 58.10.\n- Recomputed optimal fare: ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 18.0 km + 0.28 x 30.0 min) x 1.6 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.50 of on-optimal-route ERP = SGD 44.42.\n- Refund: 58.10 - 44.42 = 13.68, rounded UP to SGD 13.70.\nThat is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and 23.5% of the charge, well below the 90% share that would make it a full refund. The 1.6 surge the rider expressly accepts is carried at the figure the artifact records.\n\nERP (POL-RD-09). Two lines were billed. Kim Keat Link (2.50) lies on the optimal route and is already inside the recomputed fare. Adam Road (2.00) was off the optimal route and is ALREADY COMPREHENDED in the 13.70; under POL-RD-09(1) it is itemised for transparency and is never added on top, so the rider recovers it once and not twice. Both gantries are matched to the trace within the 250 m radius (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 8.76 m), so neither is a phantom line and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding arises.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S CONGESTION ACCOUNT. The driver says the AYE was crawling and that his route 'moved'. He names no advisory and cites no evidence ID. POL-RD-08 puts the burden on the party invoking an exculpatory clause to point to a specific artifact, and a general assertion that traffic was bad does not discharge it; the assertion is discarded and carries no weight. POL-RD-03 therefore cannot exonerate the route, and no adjusted optimal is derived. I have not escalated on the absent advisory: an exculpatory clause asserted with nothing behind it is discarded under the burden clause, not escalated, and no ruling here rests on EV-ADVIS-00114-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) — its absence is simply what defeats the excuse. POL-RD-04 (no rider instruction; both waypoint_hint fields are null), POL-RD-05 (endpoints never amended) and POL-RD-12 (solo RYDE_X trip) do not apply either. No escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 fires: the trace is unimpaired, identifiers and timestamps match, the refund is far below SGD 150.00, and there is no genuine conflict of comparable evidence.\n\nREFERRALS. None are produced. There is no repeat deviation pattern on the driver's trailing-90-day figures (1 flag over 412 completed trips) to support a POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral, and no phantom charge line to support a POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral. Consistency of the identity, distance and fare artifacts at weight 1.0 sets the confidence cap at 1.0, and my confidence is 0.90."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The one excusable explanation the driver offers is the one the record cannot test, and that matters for the disposition. The driver asserts the AYE was crawling from the Alexandra exit, and the artifact that would have decided that assertion — EV-ADVIS-00114-01 — is MISSING with weight 0.0 and carries a BLOCKING issue detail recording that no LTA advisory covers the AYE, the PIE or the Alexandra corridor in the 18:36-19:20 window. POL-RD-10(5) names precisely this situation, 'a closure asserted with no traffic_advisory', and directs escalation rather than a monetary ruling. On that reading the exoneration question is undecidable on this record, the case goes to a human with the disputed amount held rather than refunded, and I ask the chamber to prefer that route over a confident ruling on an incomplete record.",
      "side": "DRIVER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00114-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
