    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and to the driver: this ruling decides the fare for trip TRP-00114 (Bugis Junction to Jurong East MRT, 7 August 2026).\n\n1. A route deviation is established, and it is measured from the trace. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km governing where it disagrees with the trip record's rounded copy. The trace (EV-GPS-00114) runs 23.97 km against the platform's booked optimal of 18.0 km (EV-TRIP-00114) — an excess of 5.97 km, or 33.17% of optimal. That clears both establishment gates (over 0.8 km and over 20%). The deviation is NOT material: 5.97 km is below the 8.0 km figure and 33.17% is below 50%. Because it is not material, no driver-profile pattern check under POL-RD-06 is required, no FULL_REFUND uplift is available, and no driver-conduct referral arises on this trip.\n\n2. The driver's explanation does not exonerate the route. The driver says the AYE was crawling from the Alexandra exit. POL-RD-03 requires a traffic advisory naming the affected road, with a validity window and a matched shortest lawful alternative. No such advisory exists: EV-ADVIS-00114-01 is MISSING from the pool (weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), and the driver's own statement concedes 'No advisory that I know of.' A bare assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by any traffic advisory, is given no weight and does not discharge the driver's burden under POL-RD-08. Because the driver points to no artifact at all, this is not a clause invoked against an absent artifact, and POL-RD-10(5) does not fire — the exoneration question is decided against the driver, not left open. I disclose the only artifact below weight 1.0: EV-ADVIS-00114-01, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT; it is cited only for its absence, carries no fact, and neither caps confidence nor changes the outcome.\n\n3. The trace is sound. It carries 241 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps (max gap 0.0 s), no jump over 500 m and no sustained interval above 30 s. It is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07, so the excess stands on the trace without need of independent corroboration.\n\n4. The refund is arithmetic, not discretionary (POL-RD-02). The fare is METERED. The surge multiplier was read from the fare breakdown, EV-FARE-00114, where it is 1.6 — the rider accepts it and it is applied as the clause directs.\n- charged_total: SGD 58.10\n- recomputed_fare: ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 18.0 km + 0.28 x 30.0 min) x 1.6) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.50 on-route ERP = (25.70 x 1.6) + 0.80 + 2.50 = 41.12 + 0.80 + 2.50 = SGD 44.42\n- refund: 58.10 - 44.42 = SGD 13.68, rounded up to SGD 13.70.\nThat sum is returned to the rider. It is above the 0.50 de minimis floor and is 23.5% of the charge, well below the 90% share that would make it a FULL_REFUND, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND.\n\n5. ERP. Two gantries were billed, totalling 4.50. The Kim Keat Link gantry (2.50) lies on the optimal route and is carried inside the recomputed fare. The Adam Road gantry (2.00) is off the optimal route and is itemised for transparency only — it is already comprehended in the 13.70 and is NOT added on top, so it is not recovered twice. Both gantries are matched to the trace within the 250 m crossing radius (nearest fixes 0.0 m and 8.76 m), so neither is a phantom charge and no billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4) is made.\n\n6. Why not more, and why not a human. The rider contested SGD 15.00; the difference above 13.70 corresponds to no line of the fare breakdown, and POL-RD-02 does not permit a discretionary top-up to a round number. The surge the rider accepts, carried at 1.6, is why the refund is a partial rather than the whole distance difference. No escalation trigger applies: the trip identifiers match across all three core artifacts; the trace is unimpaired; timestamps are consistent; the refund is under both SGD 150.00 and charged_total; and the record is not contradicted by admissible evidence of comparable strength. The dispute is decided rather than held. The driver's route was longer with nothing to test the claimed congestion against, but the money moved is modest and the driver is not found to have acted in bad faith."
  },
